WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.810 --> 00:00:05.180
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and this week
Supernatural brought back and old friend to

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:09.350
make things right and paid off a really important
plot point setup back in season 8’s Taxi

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:10.350
Driver Episode.

00:00:10.350 --> 00:00:13.400
It also kind of showed us Dean is the world’s
worst Ghost Whisperer.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:15.750
Didn’t he learn anything from Ghostfacers?

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:20.400
I’ll also be including bits about the Spin
Off show Tribes after we speechify this episode.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.669
I’m also doing a special Fandom Oscars Event
this weekend.

00:00:23.669 --> 00:00:24.669
Be sure to subscribe to participate.

00:00:24.669 --> 00:00:25.669
It’s going to be fun.

00:00:25.669 --> 00:00:27.919
I’ll do a video to announce what the awards
are so you guys can nominate shows, movies

00:00:27.919 --> 00:00:28.919
and people.

00:00:28.919 --> 00:00:33.750
It’s going to be just like Fantasy Football
with sci-fi and fantasy shows and movies.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:37.720
So for this episode let’s do our top 5 moments,
then I’ll do my review and talk about the

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:38.820
spin off show.

00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:41.310
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
the episode yet.

00:00:41.310 --> 00:00:43.850
Number 5 - Castiel Versus Bartholomew.

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:47.880
Sure he had the B-storyline this week, but
it was a really nice twist to make the evil-ish

00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:50.430
angel Bartholomew Castiel’s former comrade
in arms.

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:54.490
If you haven’t seen it yet, the whole Raphael
war they’re talking about was from Season

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:59.080
6 which is on Netflix, but the whole exchange
they had seemed like it was setting Castiel

00:00:59.080 --> 00:01:03.000
up to become the new God either at the end
of this season or in season 10.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.299
Not in the way he was during Season 7, but
a new wiser more benevolent leader.

00:01:07.299 --> 00:01:08.770
With a lot more city miles on him.

00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:11.810
I don’t know about you guys, but I totally
wasn’t surprised when those other angels

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:13.939
showed up to follow him at the end of the
episode.

00:01:13.939 --> 00:01:16.429
Meet the newest faction in the War for heaven.

00:01:16.429 --> 00:01:18.069
Let me know what you think we should call
them.

00:01:18.069 --> 00:01:20.600
Number 4 - Tiger Mom Electrician.

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:25.260
So it was funny to see her author her own
escape via the electrical panel and Sam’s

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:26.260
reaction.

00:01:26.260 --> 00:01:29.749
But based on the timeline I feel like she
would have at least almost escaped a few times.

00:01:29.749 --> 00:01:32.340
I mean she is Tiger Mom, she’s not going
to just sit there.

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:34.850
They didn’t acknowledge attempted breakouts.

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:38.389
But I think it’s implied that she’s chained
to the opposite wall because she’s almost

00:01:38.389 --> 00:01:39.539
escaped several times.

00:01:39.539 --> 00:01:42.750
If you’re smart enough to Macgyver a control
panel you should totally be able to pick a

00:01:42.750 --> 00:01:43.750
lock.

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:46.639
Number 3 - Tiger Mom part 2, Revenge of the
Tiger Mom.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:51.450
I loved the setup for her killing Demon Del,
I knew he was working with Crowley and had

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:55.729
clearly gone fruitloops, but I didn’t realize
he was a demon till she stabbed him.

00:01:55.729 --> 00:01:59.880
So for most of that exchange I thought she
was going to revenge murder him.

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:01.590
Number 2 - Tran Family Reunion.

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:06.069
It had been teased for the entire episode
and was a huge payoff to Crowley’s lie that

00:02:06.069 --> 00:02:07.520
he killed her back in Season 8.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:12.099
I love that as dark as Supernatural gets,
it kind of takes some of the worst things

00:02:12.099 --> 00:02:13.099
back.

00:02:13.099 --> 00:02:16.590
The big tease at the end though was that Kevin’s
spirit is going to start to get twisted from

00:02:16.590 --> 00:02:18.129
staying on earth too long.

00:02:18.129 --> 00:02:20.730
his mom acknowledges it, and as happy as the
moment was.

00:02:20.730 --> 00:02:23.269
There was this really dark overtone.

00:02:23.269 --> 00:02:26.189
and my Number 1 moment - Kevin comes back.

00:02:26.189 --> 00:02:30.269
I separated this from the reunion just because
it was the biggest surprise of the episode.

00:02:30.269 --> 00:02:33.959
I was a little blown away that they revealed
him as the ghost so quickly.

00:02:33.959 --> 00:02:36.680
And at how quickly they brushed over Sam killing
him.

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:40.181
Kevin seemed like he was totally over it and
just happy to carry on in his old role of

00:02:40.181 --> 00:02:41.510
sending them on missions.

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:43.989
Albeit for a slightly more personal one this
time.

00:02:43.989 --> 00:02:47.819
Bringing him back was such a huge thing that
I was surprised they didn’t tease and haunted

00:02:47.819 --> 00:02:50.159
bunker moments in previous episodes since
the show has been back this year.

00:02:50.159 --> 00:02:53.370
But the good news is that until they fix heaven,
Kevin is stuck on earth.

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:55.630
So you know he’ll be in another episode.

00:02:55.630 --> 00:02:59.040
Now it’s your turn, let me know what your
favorite moment was and how else do you think

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:01.230
ghost Kevin is going to help them this season?

00:03:01.230 --> 00:03:05.720
Overall I gave the episode a solid B plus
for paying off two important plot points with

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:10.340
the Kevin story and teasing a major shift
in the Castiel character and the war for Heaven.

00:03:10.340 --> 00:03:14.510
Bonus points for getting rid of Bartholomew,
he was a total dick.

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:18.909
More to the Castiel story, I always kind of
view him as the conscience of the show.

00:03:18.909 --> 00:03:21.930
The one that actually considers the moral
implications of what they’re doing.

00:03:21.930 --> 00:03:25.870
So I think Misha Collins did a great job of
showing with his performance that Castiel

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:29.609
totally understands that he’s probably going
to end up having to be God or at least the

00:03:29.609 --> 00:03:31.219
leader of Heaven again.

00:03:31.219 --> 00:03:33.220
The factions are really just the first step.

00:03:33.220 --> 00:03:35.659
Eventually his will get bigger and regardless
of how it happens.

00:03:35.659 --> 00:03:37.069
He’ll be in charge eventually.

00:03:37.069 --> 00:03:40.342
I think they’re trying to imply that this
time it will be for the better.

00:03:40.342 --> 00:03:43.650
The only things I thought could have been
better were drawing out the Kevin reveal till

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:47.810
the end of the episode instead of at the beginning
and Dean felt like he almost didn’t belong

00:03:47.810 --> 00:03:48.810
in the episode.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:53.060
If they had dropped maybe five of his lines
Sam could have done the whole mission by himself.

00:03:53.060 --> 00:03:54.420
Now let’s talk some spin off!

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:57.049
They’ve finally cast the leads for Tribes.

00:03:57.049 --> 00:03:58.989
Just like the original, there are two leads.

00:03:58.989 --> 00:04:01.090
Lucien Laviscount and Nathanien Buzolic.

00:04:01.090 --> 00:04:06.230
They’re going to air a backdoor pilot episode
on April 29th as a regular Supernatural episode.

00:04:06.230 --> 00:04:10.329
It will introduce the characters and set up
what the series main arc will be in it’s

00:04:10.329 --> 00:04:11.329
first season.

00:04:11.329 --> 00:04:14.689
The show is going to be centered in Chicago
and will be like a noir-ish monster mafia

00:04:14.689 --> 00:04:16.239
crime drama.

00:04:16.239 --> 00:04:18.510
Like The Untouchables with Monsters.

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:22.109
Or you could even compare it to the way Joss
Whedon’s Angel worked in and around Los

00:04:22.109 --> 00:04:24.660
Angeles with all the different monster/demon
factions.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:26.889
Here’s some details about their characters.

00:04:26.889 --> 00:04:31.650
Laviscount will play Ennis Roth a police officer
who’s finacee is killed in a monster mafia

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:32.810
turf war.

00:04:32.810 --> 00:04:35.220
He dedicates himself to ridding Chicago of
monsters.

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:39.720
And co-star Buzolic will play David Hayden,
a shape-shifter from one of the most powerful

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:40.720
monster families.

00:04:40.720 --> 00:04:44.389
He’s given up that life and has been living
as a human, he’ll team up with Ennis to

00:04:44.389 --> 00:04:45.539
help him clean up the city.

00:04:45.539 --> 00:04:49.150
Like I said, this will all play out in an
hour long episode on April 29th.

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:54.490
Remember Fandom Oscars coming up this week,
I’ll try to post that first video tomorrow.

00:04:54.490 --> 00:04:58.050
Right now click here for my last Supernatural
video and click here to learn all about the

00:04:58.050 --> 00:04:59.800
new Flash spinoff show with Grant Gustin.

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:01.289
Thanks for watching, see you guys tonight.

00:05:01.289 --> 00:05:01.900
High Fives!

